From 02ef1a6b36cd648ece0418992cbe14e4a9709db6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 08:06:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add monochrome layer to adaptive icon (themed-icon black fix)

The color icon (background + foreground) was already confirmed correct
and visible -- verified by compositing it exactly as Android would and
rendering it at real launcher sizes. If it's still rendering solid
black after a clean uninstall/reinstall, the most likely remaining
cause is Android 13+ 'Themed icons' (Material You monochrome icon
theming): when a launcher has that turned on and an app provides no
explicit <monochrome> layer, some launchers auto-generate one from the
color icon. For artwork this dark by design (mean brightness ~25/255),
that auto-generated version can legitimately render as solid black --
independent of whether the color version is correct.

Fix: added a proper <monochrome> layer, generated mechanically from
the same frozen source pixels via edge-detection (Sobel gradient
magnitude, thresholded to drop the noise floor / film-grain texture
and keep only real silhouette/question-mark/magnifying-glass outlines,
slightly dilated so fine lines survive downscaling). This is a
deterministic derivative of the existing artwork, not new artwork --
nothing was redesigned. Verified legible at realistic small icon
sizes (32-48px).

Changed:
- app/src/main/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml: added
  <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
- app/src/main/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher_round.xml: same
- app/src/main/res/mipmap-{m,h,x,xx,xxx}hdpi/ic_launcher_monochrome.png: new

Unchanged: ic_launcher_foreground.png / ic_launcher_round.png (already
fixed and verified in the previous commit), ic_launcher.png,
AndroidManifest.xml, colors.xml, and all Java sources (verified via
git status and a clean recompile against the same Android API stub
set used throughout this project).
